m solving and responsibility may outweigh unknown cooperation, but we have no evidence of cooperation issues. However D is regarded as a know-it-all and has hot temper, which could affect crew cooperation. Candidate A has leadership and anticipation but also regarded as show-off and not open to new ideas, which could affect adaptability and crew cooperation. We need to decide whether to keep recommendation C or shift.\n\nGiven concerns about C's communication difficulty and egocentric, but still strong reliability and decision-making. The panel hasn't discussed stress resilience for A and D. B has communication issues. So C still seems strongest overall. We can support C but note concerns and ask for more info on A and D's crew cooperation. Could ask Sarah or Emily for observations on A's reliability or D's cooperation. But we can also keep vote for C.\n\nThus public message: I agree with Emily that C is strongest, but highlight communication difficulty and egocentric as serious concerns that could affect crew cooperation, and note lack of info on A and D. I maintain provisional recommendation for C, but request further info on A's reliability and D's cooperation.\n\nWe must not ask a question in public; we can ask via tool if needed. But we could ask Sarah about A's reliability. However we can also just state our position.\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: C 100% reliable, creates positive crew atmosphere, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education. Use these to argue.\n\nThus vote remains Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
